---
/**
 * The Foundation — the relationship hub.
 *
 * This page exists because NVVVF is now visible enough in the chapter's own
 * work that it deserves a top-level answer to "what is NVVVF, and how does it
 * relate to Chapter 227?" — not just a child page under Ways to Give.
 *
 * It deliberately does NOT duplicate what NVVVF's own site says about itself:
 * nvvvf.org is where a visitor learns the Foundation's full story. This page
 * exists to do the one thing nvvvf.org cannot — show a donor how the money
 * NVVVF raises actually moves once it reaches Chapter 227, and point at the
 * chapter's own itemized spending record. It also does not repeat the full
 * disputed-figures disclosure that already lives on /give/nvvvf; that stays
 * the one place those numbers are argued over, so there is a single source of
 * truth for the review conversation rather than two copies that can drift.
 */
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../components/HeroBand.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import { validateNvvvf, buildNvvvfView } from '../lib/nvvvf';
import raw from '../data/nvvvf.json';

const nvvvf = validateNvvvf(raw);
const view = buildNvvvfView(nvvvf);
---

<PageLayout
  title="The Foundation"
  description="Chapter 227 and the Northern Virginia Vietnam Veterans Foundation are separate organizations with one mission. Here's how they work together, and where a gift to the Foundation actually ends up."
  hero
>
  <HeroBand
    slot="hero"
    tone="warm"
    eyebrow="Chapter 227 & NVVVF"
    title="One mission, two organizations"
    lede="In June 2025, Chapter 227 created a separate charity — the Northern Virginia Vietnam Veterans Foundation — to raise money for one thing: getting a veteran past a sudden financial emergency before it becomes a permanent one."
    primary={{ label: 'Where Your Money Goes', href: '/give/impact' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Give to the Foundation', href: '/give/nvvvf' }}
    image={{
      src: '/images/nvvvf-partnership-wide.jpg',
      alt: 'A graphic captioned "One Mission. Two Organizations. One Commitment to Veterans." — two people shaking hands over a sunlit mountain landscape, with the Vietnam Veterans of America Chapter 227 seal and the Northern Virginia Vietnam Veterans Foundation seal side by side above them.',
      width: 1050,
      height: 700,
    }}
  />

  <!-- ---------- What it is ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>227 runs the program. The Foundation sustains it.</h2>
    <p>
      Chapter 227 has been verifying needs and paying veterans&rsquo; creditors directly since long before the
      Foundation existed. NVVVF doesn&rsquo;t run the emergency assistance program — it exists to raise the money
      that keeps the chapter&rsquo;s own program funded, so the volunteers with decades of experience doing this work
      can keep doing it.
    </p>
    <p>
      {view.fullName} is a <strong>separate 501(c)(3) corporation</strong> from Vietnam Veterans of America Chapter
      227, with its own board and its own mailing address. Chapter 227 created it, and most of its leadership also
      serves the chapter in some capacity — but legally, financially and administratively, the two are distinct.
    </p>
    <p>{nvvvf.purpose.crisisFrame}</p>
    <p class="muted note">
      Emergency financial assistance is one program among several. Chapter 227 has also run monthly member dinners,
      guest speakers and holiday events since 1985 — see <a href="/events">Events &amp; News</a> and
      <a href="/programs">What We Do</a> for the rest of what the chapter does.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- How they work together ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>How the two organizations work together</h2>
    <p><strong>{nvvvf.division.foundation}</strong> {nvvvf.division.chapter}</p>
    <p>{nvvvf.division.creditorRule}</p>
    <p>
      Requests reach the chapter through community partners, including {view.referralSentence}. Full detail on how
      to give — and the Foundation&rsquo;s tax status — is on
      <a href="/give/nvvvf">Give to the Foundation &rarr;</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- History ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Forty years, then a foundation</h2>
    <p>Chapter 227 was formed in 1985. The Foundation was created in the chapter&rsquo;s fortieth year, in {nvvvf.founded.display}.</p>
    <p>{nvvvf.succession.summary}</p>
    <p>
      The Foundation is also building a public website of its own, where it will tell its own story directly. It is
      still in development, so this page does not link to it yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ---------- The bridge ---------- -->
  <section class="stack">
    <h2>Where a gift to the Foundation ends up</h2>
    <p>
      A gift to NVVVF funds one thing: Chapter 227&rsquo;s emergency financial assistance program. The Foundation
      raises and stewards the money; the chapter&rsquo;s own volunteers verify each request and pay the veteran&rsquo;s
      landlord, utility company or repair shop directly. If you&rsquo;re considering a gift to the Foundation, the
      most direct way to see what that money supports is the chapter&rsquo;s own record of what it has paid out.
    </p>
    <p class="muted note">
      The Foundation also reports its own impact figures. Several of those numbers currently disagree across the
      Foundation&rsquo;s own source documents and have not been published here for that reason — the full disclosure
      is on <a href="/give/nvvvf">Give to the Foundation</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <CallToAction
    title="See where the chapter's own money goes"
    primary={{ label: 'Where Your Money Goes', href: '/give/impact' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Give to the Foundation', href: '/give/nvvvf' }}
    tone="clay"
  >
    An itemized, year-by-year account of every dollar Chapter 227 has paid out — the same volunteers who verify
    NVVVF-funded emergency assistance requests.
  </CallToAction>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .stack + .stack {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-block-end: var(--s-4);
  }

  .stack > p {
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
  }

  .stack > p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-4);
  }

  .note {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
  }
</style>
